From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] The GPU address lookup without the page cache is a plain walk again

MemoryManager::GpuToCpuAddress is the hottest lookup of the GPU threads. Since 0541 the page
cache (EDEN_UP_GPU_PAGE_CACHE) lived in the same function, and its cold paths (the table's first
allocation, the per-thread pointer) made the compiler set up a stack frame of six saved registers
on every lookup, with the switch off as well; before 0541 the function had no frame at all. No
fps loss was measured from it (T120 against T116, same hour), so this is tidying: under 1% at best.

- The page-table walk is a function of its own, WalkGpuToCpuAddress, always inlined.
- The cached path is GpuToCpuAddressCached, never inlined, reached by one jump when the switch
  is on (a forced tail call: as a plain call it kept the frame too). It does what the branch did: look in the per-thread table, walk on a miss, fill the slot.
- GpuToCpuAddress is the range check, the switch read and the walk. With the switch off nothing
  else runs.
- The switch is read with the new Common::LiveSwitch::Peek: one plain load. Value() carries a
  first-use check (a guard, and a call the hot path would have to keep registers for), which alone
  kept the frame in the first build of this patch. The first use is made once in the memory
  manager's constructor instead.

Behaviour is the same in both settings; the switch stays live. Check after a build: the function
must be a leaf again in the eboot (llvm-objdump: no push at its start, as in T116).

diff --git a/src/common/live_switch.h b/src/common/live_switch.h
--- a/src/common/live_switch.h
+++ b/src/common/live_switch.h
@@ -753,6 +753,15 @@
     return g_values[static_cast<size_t>(id)].load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
 }
 
+/// Value() without its first-use step: one plain load and nothing else, for a reader so hot that
+/// the first-use check (a guard and a call the compiler must keep a stack frame for) would show.
+/// The owner of the switch must have called Value<id>() once before (a constructor does), or
+/// this reads 0 for ever.
+template <Id id>
+[[nodiscard]] inline s64 Peek() noexcept {
+    return g_values[static_cast<size_t>(id)].load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
+}
